## Context and authority

Filed from replicator 0003 (branch t0003-full-chain, commit ec32d2c) at
the author's request on 2026-11-26. Integration-review finding for
tracker 1552; complements 1569 (identification review). Request for
receiving Imagine, not an implementation authorization.

## Evidence

An inventory of the robustness work in 19 I4R discussion papers (fixed
sample: 9 from replicator's 0002 development cohort, 10 drawn with seed
20261126): `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/replicator/replications/chain-pilot-0003/i4r-robustness-inventory.md`
and `.json`, sample list beside them. 15 are replication reports, 4 are
meta-science or protocol. Extraction by Sonnet-class agents; three
entries spot-checked against the source text (papers 89, 100, 137), all
held; counts are approximate. No report in the sample concerns an RDD.

Observations (counts over the 15 reports or 127 checks; see the file):
- most frequent check categories: re-coding in other software, functional
  form/estimator, alternative controls, inference/clustering, sample
  restrictions, coding-error fixes (9 checks in 7 papers);
- identification critique in 5 of 15 reports, mostly inside the
  robustness section, own section in 1;
- original estimate beside each check in about half the checks; 4
  reports never do it; original column first is the common layout.

A first draft of a Carter (2024) plan in replicator showed the overfitting
risk: an RDD menu written from one paper would have entered the skill.

## Proposed split (for Imagine to accept, amend or reject)

Into SKILL.md § probe (design-independent):
1. Inventory the paper's own robustness (appendix and code) and propose
   only checks it does not already run; list the excluded ones.
2. Every code anomaly logged by `reproduce` becomes a candidate check.
3. The plan fixes its reporting rule beforehand: every check reported, no
   overall verdict from a count of passes.
4. Drop-one at the assignment or cluster unit, not the observation.
5. Validation hygiene: in a validation run, the executor and the signers
   have not read the paper's I4R report.
6. Sign-off modes: a person's line (default); a person's approval given
   in conversation, transcribed verbatim and labelled as transcription;
   an author-authorized model panel (replicator 0003 pilots Astra +
   Fable, rule in its PROTOCOL.md), recorded as a deviation until the
   pilot result is in.

Into a new reference (`references/robustness-menus.md`), menus per
design, each item citing either at least two I4R reports in an inventory
or a named methods source:
- from the sample: meta-analysis (publication-bias adjustments,
  REML vs DerSimonian-Laird, drop-one study); DiD (alternative treatment
  thresholds, event study, multiple-testing correction over interactions);
  experiments (pre-analysis-plan deviations, controls, outliers);
  observational panels (proxy validity, dropping dominant units,
  nonlinear controls);
- from methods literature, marked as such: RDD (bandwidth grid, kernel,
  polynomial order, donut, placebo cutoffs).

Stays in the paper folder, never in the skill: any variable, unit,
threshold or check specific to one paper.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Receiving Imagine records facts, duplicates (1568, 1569), ownership,
  standing rulings (rule 4: a person signs).
- [x] If accepted: SKILL.md § probe gains the steps kept; the menus file
  exists with a source per item; no paper-specific item in either.
- [ ] The sign-off modes question is ruled after replicator 0003 reports.

## Receiving Imagine (2026-11-26)

Disposition: accept the design-independent planning and sourced-menu work for
implementation, subject to separating the pending sign-off decision. Keep the
existing person-written signature rule. No generic model-panel or transcribed
signature authorization follows from this reception, and the final sign-off
exit criterion remains open until the author rules after the pilot report.

1. **Facts against framing.** Read the inventory and PROTOCOL.md at replicator
   ec32d2c. They document extracted candidate checks, not a certified frequency
   census or a demonstrated improvement in replication quality. The inventory
   mixes reproduction operations and non-replication papers; its counts remain
   approximate and its report sample supplies no empirical RDD coverage. The
   protocol calls model-panel signing an explicit pilot deviation and describes
   a two-paper descriptive trial, not an accuracy estimate. No completed pilot
   report was present at this cited revision; no heldout I4R report was read.
2. **Duplicates and overlap.** Current probe already requires a signed fair
   plan, comparison to an original estimate, and renewed signature for changes.
   Rule 5 labels heterogeneity and extensions as extras; coding-error fixes
   already count as robustness under rule 7. Reuse those contracts. Closed1568
   covers frozen computational confirmation; closed1569 covers source-based
   identification appraisal, whose proposed empirical tests enter probe. The
   new work is inventory/exclusions before selection, sourced candidate menus,
   and prospective complete reporting.
3. **Ownership and placement.** Harness owns generic probe steps and an
   attributed reference with applicability, source per item, and explicit
   methods-literature origins for RDD. Each menu item needs two actual I4R
   report examples from an inspected inventory or a named methods source;
   inventory labels alone cannot justify a recommendation. Variables, units,
   thresholds, and case judgments stay in the paper folder. Drop-one units
   follow the design/assignment/clustering structure; observation deletion is
   not a universal influence test. Menus suggest candidates, not mandatory or
   automatically authorized checks.
4. **Standing rulings and fit.** Preserve fairness and the person-written
   signature gate. Pilot-only model signing remains a recorded deviation. For
   validation, keep executing and signing contexts unexposed to the heldout
   comparison report, disclose prior exposure, and exclude exposed papers from
   independent validation claims. Do not export this blindness restriction to
   ordinary report appraisal. Every planned check has a reported disposition
   (completed, failed, blocked, or withdrawn, with reason); amendments preserve
   their history and require renewed signature. No overall robustness verdict
   follows from a pass count. Classify heterogeneity/extensions separately even
   when an inventory or menu calls them robustness.

Blind-Spot pass: two material omissions accepted, complete disposition of
every planned check and design-specific scope classification under rule 5.
They refine existing reporting/fairness requirements without adding a verb or
a new empirical deliverable. Requested reviewer Sol6.1 medium, native OpenAI;
observed model/effort masked. No scientific rerun or paid model call occurred.

